R"VG(
# letters4.vg (H-04, the second pass): the last of a letter's ordinary life (letters2.vg's `letter.ambient`): what the writer and
# the reader remember together, the people's sayings, the neighbours, the gifts in the fold of the letter, the town, the feasts.

# ---- what they remember (to the reader alone) -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

let.remember
  (3) Do you remember {let.mem}? {let.mem.after}
  I was thinking of {let.mem} the other day. {let.mem.after}
let.mem (share=0.7)
  the winter the {herd} got into the house
  (has:$me.home.landmark) how we played {pastime} behind {$me.home.landmark}
  the {festival} when you ate all the {food} and blamed the {beast}
  the year the {crop} came up twice
  Mother's {vessel.one.n}, the one with the crack, that she would not throw away
  the night we watched {skynight} from the roof
  how you swore {oath} you would never leave {$me.home}
  the old {$me.trade} who taught us both and liked neither of us
  (desert=0) the summer we swam in {river}
  (desert=1) the summer {watersrc} ran sweet
  the song about the {beast} and the {bird.one}, and how it ended
  the {colour.holy} door of our first house
  the {let.instrument} you made from a {vessel.one.n} and a string
  how Father counted the {herd} twice and got two answers
let.mem.after
  I walked past the place yesterday on my way to {holyplace}.
  Nobody else does.
  I laughed out loud at the {craft}, thinking of it.
  I still have the scar.
  It seems a hundred years ago, and it was twenty years, with the {bird} coming back every one of them.
  The children do not believe a word of it, nor the {beast}.
  (temper=wry) You were wrong then, too.

# ---- the people's sayings -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

let.saying
  {proverb}, as Mother used to say{let.saying.tail}
  The old ones have a saying: {proverb}{let.saying.tail}
  {let.saying.lead} {proverb}{let.saying.tail}
  (temper=wry) Somebody at the market said it to me, {proverb}, as though nobody had ever said it before.
  (has:$you) You used to say it: {proverb}{let.saying.tail}

# ---- the neighbours -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

let.gossip
  (3) {let.gossip.main}{let.gossip.tail}
let.gossip.main (share=0.7)
  (has:$me.home.landmark) the {craft} people by {$me.home.landmark} have quarrelled with everyone, and then with each other {=.quarrel}
  our neighbour's {beast} ate the priest's {garment.n} {=.beast}
  (has:$me.home.quarter) two families in {$me.home.quarter} are not speaking, over {vessel.one} {=.quarrel}
  the widow who keeps the {food} stall has married again, a man half her age with a fine {garment.n} {=.wed}
  (age<=medieval) someone stole the {colour.holy} cloth from {holyplace} and brought it back washed {=.odd}
  the one who sells {fuel} has a new cart and the whole street is talking about it {=.talk}
  the {$me.trade} next door has taken to {vice} {=.vice}
  a stranger came through selling {vessel}, and half the street bought one {=.stranger}
  the schoolmaster's {beast} has been in every garden in {$me.home} {=.beast}
  everyone says the {craft} woman is a witch, because her {veg} are bigger {=.witch}
  (age<=industrial) the {craft} woman has cursed the whole street, {curse}, she says, and means it {=.odd}
  the young people dance {time.of} by {town.open}, and the old people watch from the doors and say it was better done once {=.dance}
let.gossip.tail
  (2) .
  (.quarrel=1) ; I keep out of it, mostly.
  (.beast=1) ; nobody will say whose.
  (.wed=1) ; good luck to them both.
  (.odd=1) ; we are all very confused.
  (.vice=1) ; we pretend not to notice.
  (.stranger=1) ; they are cracking already.
  (.witch=1) ; I have asked her for seed.
  (.dance=1) ; it was not.

# ---- the gifts in the fold of the letter (to the reader) -----------------------------------------------------------------

let.gift
  (3) {let.gift.main}{let.gift.tail}
let.gift.main (share=0.8)
  I send you {vessel.one} of {food} with this {=.food}
  the {garment.n} you sent fits, more or less {=.fit}
  I am sending the {let.tool.n} back; it is the best I ever borrowed {=.tool}
  there is {crop2} seed in the fold of this letter, from our own plot {=.seed}
  (age>=industrial) I have put a little money in with this; do not argue {=.money}
  (age>=medieval age<=medieval) the {smallcoin} in the knot of the cord is for you {=.money}
  the {colour.any} thread you asked for is in with this {=.thread}
  I have nothing to send but this letter and the smell of {fuel} on it {=.nothing}
let.gift.tail
  (2) .
  (.food=1) ; eat it before it walks.
  (.food=1) ; share it, or do not.
  (.fit=1) ; I wear it to {holyplace} and feel very grand.
  (.seed=1) ; plant it by the door and see what it thinks of you.
  (.money=1) ; spend it on something foolish.
  (.thread=1) ; it was the last in the market.
  (.nothing=1) .

# ---- the town -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

let.town
  (3) {let.town.main}{let.town.tail}
let.town.main (share=0.75)
  (has:$me.home.landmark) the mending at {$me.home.landmark} is done, and everything there looks worse {=.mend}
  they have moved the market to {town.open} {=.moved}
  (has:$me.home.landmark) a new {craft} shop has opened by {$me.home.landmark} {=.shop}
  (edge=walls) they are mending {town.edge} again, with stones from the old houses {=.wall}
  the new wall by {town.open} is {n} {measure.far} long and leans already {=.mend}
  (streets=organic) a cart got stuck in {streets.of} for a whole day {=.cart}
  (streets=grid) they have numbered the streets, and nobody uses the numbers {=.numbers}
  (public=gardens) the gardens are in flower, and the {bird} are drunk on them {=.garden}
  (has:$me.home.ptrade) all anyone talks of {season.this} is {$me.home.ptrade} {=.talk}
  (age>=industrial inv.electric=1) they have put lights in {town.open}, and nobody sleeps {=.lights}
  (age<=medieval) the crier at {town.open} is new, and nobody believes a word of it yet {=.crier}
  (tops=statues) somebody climbed up and put a {garment.n} on one of the statues on the roofs, and it is still there {=.statue}
  (links=arcades) the arcades are full of {craft} stalls since the rain {=.shop}
let.town.tail
  (2) .
  (.mend=1) ; it was better broken.
  (.moved=1) ; the old place is all weeds and memory.
  (.shop=1) ; the owner is from {city} and lets everyone know it.
  (.wall=1) ; the old houses are sorry to see them go.
  (.cart=1) ; the whole town came to advise.
  (.lights=1) ; the {bird} are confused, and so am I.
  (.statue=1) ; it suits it.

# ---- the feasts -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

let.feast
  (3) {let.feast.main}{let.feast.tail}
let.feast.main (share=0.75)
  {festival} is coming, and with it {feast.custom} {=.coming}
  we kept {festival} with {feast.custom}, as always {=.kept}
  the young ones are practising for {feast.custom} {=.practice}
  this year I am to carry the {colour.holy} cloth at {festival}, which is an honour and a weight {=.honour}
  there were games at {festival}, {pastime} and the rest, and our street won for once {=.won}
  (age>=industrial) {festival} has gone to the shops; there are {vessel} of {food} for sale on every corner {=.sold}
  we wore {colour.holy} for {festival}, as the old way is, and the young ones wore what they liked {=.old}
let.feast.tail
  (2) .
  (.coming=1) ; the house smells of {food} already.
  (.kept=1) ; it rained, as it always does.
  (.practice=1) ; we hear them through the walls.
  (.won=1) ; nobody will ever hear the end of it.
  (.sold=1) ; Mother would have hated it.
  (.old=1) .
)VG"
